## Usage Examples

### Basic Chart

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={data}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Study Hours vs Exam Score',
    chartSubtitleValue: 'Correlation between study time and test performance.',
  }}
/>
```

### With Legend and DataDisplay

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={multiSeriesData}
  chartLegend={true}
  dataDisplay={true}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Marketing vs Sales',
    chartSubtitleValue: 'Regional comparison.',
  }}
  dataDisplayConfig={{
    mainLabelValue: 'Total data points',
    dataHead: { dataLeadValue: '20' },
  }}
  scatterPlotGroupConfig={{
    yAxisConfig: {
      yAxisLabel: true,
      yAxisLabelValue: 'Revenue (£k)',
    },
    xAxisConfig: {
      xAxisLabel: true,
      xAxisLabelValue: 'Spend (£k)',
    },
  }}
/>
```

### Full Width

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={data}
  fullWidth={true}
  height={460}
  chartLegend={true}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Regional Performance',
  }}
  scatterPlotGroupConfig={{
    dotSize: 14,
    yAxisConfig: {
      tickCount: 5,
      formatValue: (v) => `${v}%`,
      yAxisLabel: true,
      yAxisLabelValue: 'Revenue (%)',
    },
    xAxisConfig: {
      tickCount: 5,
      formatValue: (v) => `${v}k`,
      xAxisLabel: true,
      xAxisLabelValue: 'Spend (£k)',
    },
  }}
/>
```

### Interactive with Hover Callback

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={data}
  interactive={true}
  onDotHover={(hoverData) => {
    if (hoverData.isHovered) {
      console.log(`Focused: ${hoverData.label ?? `Point ${hoverData.index + 1}`}`);
    }
  }}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Interactive Scatter',
  }}
/>
```

### Categorical Hover (Dim by Series)

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={multiSeriesData}
  interactive={true}
  chartLegend={true}
  scatterPlotGroupConfig={{
    hoverType: 'categorical',
  }}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Regional Comparison',
  }}
/>
```

### With HoverBadge

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={data}
  interactive={true}
  scatterPlotGroupConfig={{
    hoverBadge: true,
    hoverType: 'individual',
    yAxisConfig: { yAxisLabelValue: 'Revenue (£k)' },
    xAxisConfig: { xAxisLabelValue: 'Spend (£k)' },
  }}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Scatter with HoverBadge',
  }}
/>
```

### Animated Entry

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={data}
  animated={true}
  interactive={true}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Animated Scatter',
  }}
/>
```

### With Data-Driven Sizing

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={sizedData}
  interactive={true}
  chartLegend={true}
  scatterPlotGroupConfig={{
    sizeRange: [6, 28],
    hoverBadge: true,
    yAxisConfig: { yAxisLabelValue: 'Revenue (£k)' },
    xAxisConfig: { xAxisLabelValue: 'Spend (£k)' },
  }}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Bubble Scatter',
    chartSubtitleValue: 'Dot size represents market cap.',
  }}
/>
```

When data points include a `size` field, dot radii are automatically scaled via `d3.scaleSqrt()`. The `sizeRange` prop sets the min/max diameter in pixels (default `[6, 24]`). Points without `size` receive the minimum radius.

### Animated with Dataset Switching

```tsx
const [activeDataSet, setActiveDataSet] = useState<'A' | 'B'>('A');

<ScatterPlotChart
  data={activeDataSet === 'A' ? datasetA : datasetB}
  animated={true}
  interactive={true}
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: 'Data Transition Demo',
  }}
/>;
```

When `animated={true}`, switching data triggers smooth transitions: shared dots (matched by `id`) move to new positions and smoothly resize, new dots fade in at their target radius (opacity only), and removed dots fade out at their original radius (opacity only).

### Minimal (No Header/Footer)

```tsx
<ScatterPlotChart
  data={data}
  width={400}
  height={300}
  chartHeader={false}
  chartFooter={false}
  scatterPlotGroupConfig={{
    dotSize: 10,
    yAxisConfig: { tickCount: 5 },
    xAxisConfig: { tickCount: 5 },
  }}
/>
```

## Design Tokens Used

| Property          | CSS Custom Property                     | Purpose                         |
| ----------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Section gap       | `var(--Spacing-5)`                      | Gap between major sections      |
| Categorical color | `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-1..12)` | Dot and legend item fill color  |

> Color index is clamped to `[1, 12]`. All tokens are injected at `:root` by the DataVis CSS pipeline (`generateDataVisCSS` → `useStyleInjection` at `@layer brand`) and always available at render time — no JS resolution required.

## Token Pipeline

```
generateDataVisCSS()
  → injects --DataVis-Categorical-Bold-{1..12} at @layer brand

getCategoricalColor(index) in ScatterPlotChart
  → returns `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-${clamp(index, 1, 12)})`
  → used by legend auto-generation + per-dot fill

var(--Spacing-5) in container inline style
  → resolved by CSS cascade from OneUI token layer
```

## Legend Auto-Generation

When `chartLegend` is `true` and no `chartLegendConfig.items` or `chartLegendConfig.categoryLabelValue` is provided:

1. Extracts unique `series` values from `ScatterPlotDataPoint[]`
2. Creates one legend item per series using `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-{index})` CSS vars
3. If no `series` field is present, a single "Series 1" entry is created with color index 1

## Height Behavior

The `height` prop controls the **total chart container height** (default 270px). The outer flex-column container is set to this height, and the ScatterPlotGroup fills the remaining space after header, legend, DataDisplay, and footer are laid out at their natural auto heights.

```
┌───────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ChartHeader (title + subtitle)       │  ← Auto height
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ChartLegend (optional)               │  ← Auto height
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│  DataDisplay (optional)               │  ← Auto height
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                       │
│          ScatterPlotGroup             │  ← flex: 1 (fills remaining)
│    YAxis │ plotWrapper (SVG circles)  │
│          │ XAxis                      │
│          └── HoverBadge (tooltip)     │
│                                       │
├───────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ChartFooter (source + notes)         │  ← Auto height
└───────────────────────────────────────┘
      Total height: `height` prop
```

## Accessibility

Wrapped by `ChartAccessibility` (enabled by default). Uses `chartType="scatter"`. Provides:

- ARIA attributes: `role="figure"`, `aria-label`, `aria-describedby`
- Auto-generated natural language summary from scatter data
- Visually-hidden data table for screen reader navigation (uses `y` value as the primary metric, `label` or `series` as category)
- Statistics: min, max, avg, trend detection
- `accessibilityContainerStyle` forwarded to the `ChartAccessibility` wrapper so `fullWidth`, string `width`, and string `height` propagate through the `role="figure"` div

### Interactive Accessibility Layers

When `interactive={true}` (default), three additional layers are activated:

**1. Keyboard Navigation (`useRovingTabIndex`)**

All data points form a single tab stop. Arrow keys move focus between points (Left/Right, wraps). Home/End jump to first/last. The chart calls `onDotHover` automatically on focus changes.

**2. Screen Reader Announcements (`useChartAccessibility`)**

Hover and keyboard focus build live text from point data:

```
"Point 3: x 25, y 60"                               // no label, no axis labels
"Point 3: Marketing Spend (£k) 25, Revenue (£k) 60" // with xAxisLabelValue + yAxisLabelValue
"London: x 25, y 60"                                // with label, no axis labels
"North: Revenue (£k) 25, Spend (£k) 60"             // with series + axis labels
```

The `useChartAccessibility` hook accepts `{ rawLiveText, width, height, isFullWidth }` and returns `{ liveText, accessibilityContainerStyle, dataDisplayId }`. The debounced `liveText` is passed to `ChartAccessibility` via the `liveText` prop.

The `x`/`y` values in this text prefer `xAxisConfig.valueFormat`/`yAxisConfig.valueFormat` over the plain `formatValue` function on either axis — matching the precedence ScatterPlotGroup itself uses for the visible tick labels, so setting `valueFormat` alone keeps the announcement and the ticks in sync.

**3. Focusable Data Points + Proximity Overlay (in ScatterPlotGroup)**

Each point gets an invisible `role="button"` div (`pointerEvents: none`) with `aria-label`, `aria-roledescription="data point"`, and `aria-controls` linking to the DataDisplay when present. These divs are **keyboard-only** — hit areas are sized to at least 44×44px (WCAG 2.5.5) for focus ring targeting.

Mouse interactions are handled separately by a **Delaunay proximity overlay** — a single `aria-hidden` div covering the full plot area. On every `mousemove`, `d3.Delaunay.find()` returns the geometrically nearest dot regardless of DOM stacking order, ensuring that overlapping and clustered dots are always reachable by the cursor.

### Interactive Prop Flow

```
ScatterPlotChart (interactive=true, default)
  → effectiveInteractive = interactive && (groupConfig.interactive !== false)
    → ScatterPlotGroup (interactive, onDotHover, ariaControlsId)
      → useRovingTabIndex (keyboard nav)
      → focus overlay with role="button" elements
  → useChartAccessibility({ rawLiveText, width, height, isFullWidth })
    → ChartAccessibility (liveText, accessibilityContainerStyle)
```

### Animated Prop Flow

The `animated` prop flows directly from ScatterPlotChart to ScatterPlotGroup (not via `scatterPlotGroupConfig`). It controls both entry animation and data transition animation:

```
ScatterPlotChart (animated=false, default)
  → ScatterPlotGroup (animated)
    → useEntryAnimation (entryAnimated, entryTokens)
    │   → SVG circles: opacity 0 → 1 with stagger delay  [--Motion-Duration-L, --Motion-Easing-Entrance-Moderate]
    → useDataTransition (dataTransitionTokens)            [--Motion-Duration-L, --Motion-Easing-Transition-Moderate]
    → useExitAnimation (exitTokens)                       [--Motion-Duration-S, --Motion-Easing-Exit-Moderate]
        → On data change (after entry settled, render-phase diffing):
          → Shared dots (id in both datasets):
              CSS cx/cy/r/opacity transition to new position, scale, opacity
          → Entering dots (id only in new data):
              Start at opacity=0, r=0 at final position.
              Transition: opacity 0→1, r 0→targetR  (fade-in + scale-up)
          → Exiting dots (id only in old data):
              Snapshot cx/cy/r captured from pre-change scale before domain updates.
              Rendered at snapshot position. Transition: opacity 1→0 (fade-out only, no position snap)
              Removed from DOM after exit fade completes.
```

See **[ChartAccessibility.md](./ChartAccessibility.md)** for full configuration.

